index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..97bf522dc906dee881f82450532417c124223720
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/native-perf-reproduce.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Reproduce native before/after measurements
+
+Use Linux x86-64, Bun 1.4.3, an existing Xvfb and the same system fonts and
+hardware for both binaries. Obtain baseline and candidate artifacts with their
+source/toolchain/hash receipts. Both apps must use LLVM 19, `-O3`,
+`BACKPLANE_LOW_MEM=1`, `BACKPLANE_JOBS=2` and `BACKPLANE_GOOGLE_BAKE=0`.
+Check the actual binary hashes against those receipts before running. Build
+the shared helper before taking measurements, if it is not already available:
+
+```sh
+mkdir -p build
+cc -O2 test/tools/xpoke.c -o build/xpoke -lX11
+bun test/tools/perf_fixture_test.ts
+# Requires an already-built production shared-client bridge:
+bun test/tools/perf_fixture_codec_test.ts mobile/build/assets/bridge.js
+```
+
+Generate the same fixture for both apps. It contains 12 history threads, 1,500
+messages, two local bot threads, their bot events, a room and an uberbot. The
+history-only predecessor lacked the room/uberbot required by normal mode; its
+failed workload is not valid performance acceptance. The current generated
+fixture is **1,520 events, 556,794 bytes**, SHA-256
+`ac5f4374d7946569b420d7b2ca2d5890c99d54d323a819a6d66beaf2d824b543`.
+No copied user history or provider credentials are needed.
+
+```sh
+OUT=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/bp-native-comparison.XXXXXX")
+bun test/tools/perf_fixture.ts "$OUT/fixture.jsonl" > "$OUT/fixture-receipt.json"
+sha256sum "$OUT/fixture.jsonl"
+```
+
+Set `BASE_BIN` and `CAND_BIN` to the downloaded native `dist/backplane` files,
+and set `BASE_SOURCE` and `CAND_SOURCE` to their full 40-character source labels.
+Save the original artifact receipts alongside the results. For a CI-applied
+snapshot, the candidate label is the immutable **input commit containing the
+patch**; also retain its checkout commit, expected applied tree, patch hash and
+artifact hash. An older product HEAD does not identify an uncommitted snapshot.
+The declared labels/flags in a report do not substitute for artifact receipts.
+
+The following four fresh processes share the same fixture, driver, helper and
+flags. Run them serially while holding the actual build/measurement lock.
+The dedicated displays and ports must be unused; the driver refuses to share
+an existing display. It creates private app homes and stand-in executables.
+Do not pass a live log or an installed app path.
+
+```bash
+[[ $BASE_SOURCE =~ ^[0-9a-f]{40}$ && $CAND_SOURCE =~ ^[0-9a-f]{40}$ ]] || exit 2
+FLAGS='LLVM=19;CFLAGS=-O3;LOW_MEM=1;JOBS=2;GOOGLE_BAKE=0'
+sha256sum "$BASE_BIN" "$CAND_BIN" build/xpoke test/tools/perf_load.ts \
+  test/tools/native_display.ts test/tools/native_display_compare.ts > "$OUT/inputs.sha256"
+(
+  exec 9>/tmp/bp-wt-build.lock
+  flock -x 9
+  run() {
+    side=$1; mode=$2; binary=$3; source=$4; display=$5; port=$6
+    dir="$OUT/$side-$mode"; mkdir -p "$dir/tmp" "$dir/controller-home"
+    phases=(--phases idle,bg,fg,type,input-display,open,normal --pixel-inputs)
+    [[ $mode = cold ]] || phases=(--phases open --pixel-opens)
+    code=0
+    env TMPDIR="$dir/tmp" HOME="$dir/controller-home" LANG=C.UTF-8 LC_ALL=C.UTF-8 \
+      bun test/tools/perf_load.ts --bin "$binary" --log "$OUT/fixture.jsonl" \
+      --xpoke "$PWD/build/xpoke" --xvfb /usr/bin/Xvfb --exclusive-display \
+      --display "$display" --port "$port" --agents 10 --secs 5 \
+      --source-sha "$source" --build-flags "$FLAGS" "${phases[@]}" \
+      --out "$dir/raw.json" --keep > "$dir/stdout.log" 2> "$dir/stderr.log" || code=$?
+    printf '%s\n' "$code" > "$dir/execution.exit"
+  }
+  run baseline cold "$BASE_BIN" "$BASE_SOURCE" :91 3891
+  run candidate cold "$CAND_BIN" "$CAND_SOURCE" :92 3892
+  run baseline warm "$BASE_BIN" "$BASE_SOURCE" :91 3891
+  run candidate warm "$CAND_BIN" "$CAND_SOURCE" :92 3892
+  for surface in input title; do
+    mode=cold; [[ $surface = input ]] || mode=warm
+    code=0
+    bun test/tools/native_display_compare.ts "$OUT/baseline-$mode/raw.json" \
+      "$OUT/candidate-$mode/raw.json" --out "$OUT/compare-$surface.json" \
+      > "$OUT/compare-$surface.log" 2>&1 || code=$?
+    printf '%s\n' "$code" > "$OUT/compare-$surface.exit"
+  done
+)
+```
+
+The configured five seconds applies to timed phases. Typing, displayed input,
+opens and normal mode run fixed event workloads and take longer. Do not stop
+the candidate because the baseline misses a budget. Keep every run's execution
+exit, phase checks and missing-sample verdicts. A zero driver exit does not mean
+every target passed. Each comparison needs exit zero **and** a parsed `pass`
+verdict with the expected identities; file existence alone proves nothing.
+
+The cold run does not calibrate the ten thread-open targets before measuring
+their first visits. Input-display separately warms its composer glyphs during
+calibration, then observes all 132 additions/Backspaces at the X-server boundary.
+The separate warm run calibrates titles and observes ten opens. Reference
+comparisons require all 12 composer prefixes or all 21 title targets and reject
+self-consistent candidate calibration errors relative to the baseline. Existing
+direct fresh-render glyph regressions remain a separate correctness anchor.
+
+Preserve the original targets: frame p99 8 ms, streaming/input 16 ms, open 50 ms
+and agent-line p99 2 ms. Report failing baseline and candidate results explicitly.
+The normal workload's **Status tab remains visually unverified** (`null` check).
+The observers cover the selected title and an ASCII composer region, not the
+entire timeline, other UI regions, compositor, physical input or scanout.
+
+Keep raw reports, traces and demand journals outside Git. A reviewable report
+should contain source/artifact/fixture hashes, the actual flags/toolchain and
+hardware, sample counts, per-phase p99/max values, budget verdicts, independent
+reference verdicts and links to the raw artifacts. Do not commit large traces or
+claim simulator/microbenchmark results establish whole-app or physical budgets.
diff --git a/docs/perf-bench.md b/docs/perf-bench.md
index 8411f2567f83f62f14b9fb8b006b8996356346a2..98aa55cb6f733672aeb0abf2aa339ee400f2c324 100644
--- a/docs/perf-bench.md
+++ b/docs/perf-bench.md
@@ -146,3 +146,83 @@ identifies the bot's thread but does not expose its tab or open mail.
 The Mailroom pane reuses PW with `Mm.mail` as its key. Bot panes bypass
 MainM, so the existing `ui.layout.mm.hit` metric does not measure that
 pane cache; do not claim Mailroom cache hit coverage from that metric.
+
+## Native displayed-content observations
+
+`--pixel-opens` adds independent X-server title-region readback through
+`xpoke pixels X Y W H`. The driver records a demand before dispatching Return
+and polls the exact expected SHA-256 of the title pixels. A stale or different
+thread header cannot complete that demand. The region must distinguish all
+calibrated target threads and remain stable during calibration. Raw reports
+include each demand revision, expected thread, region, observed digest,
+sample count and elapsed dispatch-to-readback time. This includes input queue
+waiting and observer overhead, unlike `ui.input` processing spans.
+
+Calibration visits every target before timing. These are explicitly **warm
+opens** (`native_display.open_cache = warm-calibrated`); use a separate run
+without this option for cold-cache processing measurements. The title region
+establishes the shown thread title only. It does not certify all timeline
+content, compositor presentation, scanout, Status-tab coverage, or physical
+input latency. These observations do not enable the unfinished #232 release
+or deployment gates. `bun test/tools/native_display_test.ts` checks accepted
+changes plus stale, wrong-target, and indistinguishable-content controls.
+
+
+`--phases input-display --pixel-inputs` adds a separate 132-event input
+workload while the same ten stand-in agents stream. It calibrates the exact
+composer glyph pixels for every prefix of `Backplane42` and the empty draft,
+then types and erases the probe six times at eight events per second. Each
+independent demand starts before its X event is dispatched and completes only
+when its exact expected prefix reaches the X-server composer region. Prefixes
+must have stable, pairwise-distinct digests after caret normalization; a region
+that misses the text cannot pass calibration. The default region at 1400x900
+is `444,788,600,32`; `--composer-roi X,Y,W,H` makes any explicit adjustment
+visible in every demand. This phase keeps the original 60-key `type` workload
+and its processing measurements separately available.
+
+Only the two solid theme caret colors are replaced with their corresponding
+panel colors before hashing the ASCII probe. All glyph pixels remain compared,
+so blinking alone cannot satisfy a missing letter. The observer test preserves
+both themes' glyph pixels, rejects missing/corrupt glyph pixels and wrong PPM
+shape, and checks stale/wrong/late demands. Raw reports retain each expected
+draft, key, region, digest, sample count and dispatch-to-readback duration;
+`displayed_input_ms` applies the unchanged 16 ms p99 target and requires all
+132 events. Calibration warms glyphs. These measurements include driver process
+startup and independent readback overhead, and establish only this composer
+region's content at the X server. They do not establish physical keyboard,
+window compositor, full timeline or scanout latency.
+
+
+Compare independently captured baseline/candidate pixel references before
+accepting the displayed latency results:
+
+```sh
+bun test/tools/native_display_compare.ts baseline-input.json candidate-input.json --out input-pixels.json
+bun test/tools/native_display_compare.ts baseline-warm-opens.json candidate-warm-opens.json --out open-pixels.json
+bun test/tools/native_display_compare_test.ts
+```
+
+Both runs must supply `--source-sha FULL_40_CHARACTER_COMMIT` and the same
+explicit `--build-flags 'LLVM19 -O3 LOW_MEM=1 JOBS=1'` label, matching the actual
+builds. Reports include detected machine identity, observer schema, probe,
+repeat count, ROIs, normalization and SHA-256 hashes of the fixture, driver,
+observer, xpoke and binary. The comparison requires exact reference digests
+and identical experiment metadata, complete ordered demands, and correct
+observed digests. A candidate cannot pass by learning its own consistently
+wrong glyph or title pixels. Separate reports may cover input and opens;
+each enabled surface must be complete. This compares with the independent
+baseline, and does not replace direct fresh-render correctness checks or any
+latency target. The comparator's 29 controls exercise healthy comparisons,
+self-consistent wrong content, invalid/missing observations and changed
+experiment identities.
+
+`BP_NATIVE_VALIDATE_LOCKED=1 scripts/validate-native-glyph.sh ABSOLUTE_LOG_DIR`
+is the candidate's centralized validation entry point when the caller holds
+`/tmp/bp-wt-build.lock`; otherwise omit that variable and the script acquires
+the lock. Run it inside the parent's bounded-memory queue. It runs full
+check/proof, every original unit test, independent X-server readback, the real
+native glyph benchmark and native localization smoke tests. The glyph benchmark
+must contain all 705 uniquely indexed samples; raw microseconds and summaries
+are retained. Set `BACKPLANE_X11` and `BACKPLANE_TEST_XVFB` when using an extracted
+X11 toolchain. It does not build or run the whole app; whole-app baseline and
+candidate runs remain separately required.
